1
00:00:07,230 --> 00:00:10,790
A tourist changes dollars into another currency.

2
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:14,540
The money changer's rule is simple: multiply by 4.

3
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:16,890
So 5 dollars becomes 20.

4
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:18,360
Someone receives 36.

5
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:20,840
How many dollars did they hand in?

6
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:24,580
Pause the video and work it out.

7
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:27,660
We know what came out, so we work backwards.

8
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:31,360
The opposite of multiply by 4 is divide by 4.

9
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:33,220
36 divided by 4 is 9.

10
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:35,980
They handed in 9 dollars.

11
00:00:36,030 --> 00:00:39,940
Remember: every operation has an inverse that undoes it.

12
00:00:39,990 --> 00:00:41,360
Add undoes subtract.

13
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:43,540
Multiply undoes divide.

14
00:00:43,590 --> 00:00:48,490
If 7 times 6 is 42, then 42 divided by 6 is 7.

15
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:51,930
A function is a rule that links 2 sets of numbers.

16
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:55,440
A function machine shows the rule in a box.

17
00:00:55,490 --> 00:00:57,980
The numbers that go in are the inputs.

18
00:00:58,030 --> 00:01:01,330
The numbers that come out are the outputs.

19
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:03,260
Put 2 into this machine.

20
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:04,380
2 plus 3 is 5.

21
00:01:04,430 --> 00:01:06,460
Put in 6, and out comes 9.

22
00:01:06,510 --> 00:01:09,580
Each input has exactly 1 output.

23
00:01:09,630 --> 00:01:10,300
Your turn.

24
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:13,460
The input is 8, and the machine subtracts 3.

25
00:01:13,510 --> 00:01:14,830
What is the output?

26
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:18,170
Pause the video and try it.

27
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:19,470
8 minus 3 is 5.

28
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:21,400
The output is 5.

29
00:01:21,450 --> 00:01:25,630
A mapping diagram shows the same function with 2 number lines.

30
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:29,190
An arrow goes from each input to its output.

31
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:33,790
For the machine plus 3, every arrow moves 3 places to the right.

32
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:36,350
The arrows are all parallel.

33
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:42,330
If you know the output, run the machine backwards, using the inverse operation.

34
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:46,450
The inverse machine for multiply by 4 is divide by 4.

35
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,180
36 goes in, and 9 comes out.

36
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:49,920
Your turn.

37
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:51,180
A machine adds 7.

38
00:01:51,230 --> 00:01:52,440
The output is 12.

39
00:01:52,490 --> 00:01:53,850
What was the input?

40
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:57,250
Pause the video and try it.

41
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:00,380
The inverse of add 7 is subtract 7.

42
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:01,810
12 minus 7 is 5.

43
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:03,240
The input was 5.

44
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:05,750
Check: 5 plus 7 is 12.

45
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,080
Here is the method.

46
00:02:07,130 --> 00:02:11,920
Step 1: to find an output, put the input through the machine.

47
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:17,080
Step 2: to find an input, use the inverse operation on the output.

48
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:21,080
Step 3: to find the rule, compare the inputs and outputs.

49
00:02:21,130 --> 00:02:23,940
Try adding, then try multiplying.

50
00:02:23,990 --> 00:02:27,150
Step 4: test your rule on every pair.

51
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:29,410
This machine multiplies by 5.

52
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:31,360
Find the missing numbers.

53
00:02:31,410 --> 00:02:32,530
1 goes to what?

54
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:33,700
3 goes to what?

55
00:02:33,750 --> 00:02:35,810
And what goes to 40?

56
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:37,420
1 times 5 is 5.

57
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:39,680
3 times 5 is 15.

58
00:02:39,730 --> 00:02:42,330
For the last one, work backwards.

59
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:44,010
40 divided by 5 is 8.

60
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:45,840
The input was 8.

61
00:02:45,890 --> 00:02:47,940
This machine subtracts 6.

62
00:02:47,990 --> 00:02:50,380
The outputs are 4, 11 and 19.

63
00:02:50,430 --> 00:02:52,270
Find the inputs.

64
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:54,880
The inverse machine adds 6.

65
00:02:54,930 --> 00:02:56,630
4 plus 6 is 10.

66
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,490
11 plus 6 is 17.

67
00:02:58,540 --> 00:03:00,350
19 plus 6 is 25.

68
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:04,280
The inputs are 10, 17 and 25.

69
00:03:04,330 --> 00:03:08,500
A one-step machine maps 2 to 8, 3 to 9, and 5 to 11.

70
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:10,760
What is the function?

71
00:03:10,810 --> 00:03:11,660
2 goes to 8.

72
00:03:11,710 --> 00:03:15,430
That could be add 6, or it could be multiply by 4.

73
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:17,710
One pair is not enough.

74
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:18,730
Test add 6.

75
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,860
3 plus 6 is 9, correct.

76
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:23,640
5 plus 6 is 11, correct.

77
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:25,260
Test multiply by 4.

78
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:27,230
3 times 4 is 12, not 9.

79
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,930
So the function is add 6.

80
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:31,590
A machine divides by 4.

81
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:32,750
The output is 6.

82
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:33,840
Find the input.

83
00:03:33,890 --> 00:03:35,430
Here is Tia's working.

84
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:38,010
Which line goes wrong first?

85
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:39,180
Line 2 is wrong.

86
00:03:39,230 --> 00:03:41,600
To go backwards, use the inverse.

87
00:03:41,650 --> 00:03:45,370
The inverse of divide by 4 is multiply by 4.

88
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:46,960
6 times 4 is 24.

89
00:03:47,010 --> 00:03:48,540
The input is 24.

90
00:03:48,590 --> 00:03:51,870
Check: 24 divided by 4 is 6.

91
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,610
You use function machines every day.

92
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:59,130
To change inches into centimetres, multiply by 2.54.

93
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:03,010
In winter, the time in Hanoi is 7 hours ahead of London.

94
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:07,220
London time goes in, add 7, and Hanoi time comes out.

95
00:04:07,270 --> 00:04:13,530
And to go from Hanoi time back to London time, use the inverse machine: subtract 7.

96
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:14,790
One last question.

97
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,400
A machine divides by 2.

98
00:04:16,450 --> 00:04:17,520
The output is 9.

99
00:04:17,570 --> 00:04:18,850
What was the input?

100
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:22,130
Pause the video and answer.

101
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:25,930
The inverse of divide by 2 is multiply by 2.

102
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:27,320
9 times 2 is 18.

103
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:29,340
The input was 18.

104
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:33,490
To remember: a function machine turns inputs into outputs.

105
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:35,770
Each input has 1 output.

106
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:39,490
A mapping diagram shows a function with arrows.

107
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:43,910
To find an input, use the inverse operation on the output.

108
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:46,900
To find a rule, test it on every pair.

109
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:52,070
Great work! Now practise lesson 9.4 on Camday.
